# Star Map architecture (pointer)

Full law: [`docs/docs/architecture/star-map.md`](../../docs/docs/architecture/star-map.md).

**Permanent decision:** one **Star System** ↔ one **Star Map**. A project may
author many systems. The map is the ecliptic catalog of stations, planets,
moons, waypoints, POIs (create + assign prefab for load-on-arrival), missions,
and **Warp Gates** (AsteronEngine). Authors **right-click the map → Add** to
place any catalog kind at the cursor. Hab/Hangar stay ownership on station
entries, not map markers. Code aliases: `SystemDocument`, System Map tab,
`*.system.json`. Open Space uses the active system's map at 1:1 meters.
**Cross-system travel:** place a Warp Gate prefab with `warp-gate`
(`targetSystemId`); fly or quantum *to* it; gate swaps the Open Space host —
see [Space traversal](../../docs/docs/architecture/space-traversal.md).

When changing system documents, map authoring, POIs, Warp Gates, or
multi-system selection, read the full doc first. Also listed in `AGENTS.md`.
